      "bytes": 1412932,
      "level": "Moderate",
      "intent": "Offer an optional Visual / Source / Split switch with a source pane and read-only preview side by side in Split. Use shared heading markers and preserve the selected source location. Pins: 1 optional split view; 2 visible correspondence between source and preview; 3 one document and one undo history remain the design constraint. Split is a new proposal.",
      "annotations": [
        "Optional split view",
        "Visible correspondence between source and preview",
        "One document and one undo history remain the design constraint"
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": ".vscode-test/visual-fidelity/references/11-source-recommended.png",
      "sha256": "ea3398ed655e808f02b8f9d816093ba941cfbef83ca20f3391ada466a9f68c1f",
      "width": 1491,
      "height": 1055,
      "bytes": 1056854,
      "level": "Recommended",
      "intent": "Keep the existing Source textarea and document outline. Replace the ambiguous icon-only mode control with a clearly selected Visual / Source segmented switch, label Open in VS Code separately, and visibly dim unavailable visual-formatting commands while Source is active. Add no syntax-editor features. Pins: 1 current mode is explicit; 2 host text editor is a distinct action; 3 commands communicate context.",
      "annotations": [
        "Current mode is explicit",
        "Host text editor is a distinct action",
        "Commands communicate context"
      ]
    }
  ],
